    {
      "text": "shall deny me before men, him will I also deny, Matt. 10:33 (Luke 12:9). let him deny himself, Matt. 16:24 (Mark 8:34; Luke 9:23). cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice, Matt. 26:34 (26:75; Mark 14:30, 72; Luke 22:34, 61; John 13:38). he denied before them all, Matt. 26:70 (Mark 14:68; Luke 22:57). he confessed, and denied not, John 1:20. Peter then denied again: and immediately the cock crew, John 18:27. denied the faith, and is worse than an infidel, 1 Tim. 5:8. if we deny him, he also will deny us, 2 Tim. 2:12. form of godliness, but denying the power, 2 Tim. 3:5. in works they deny him, Titus 1:16. denying ungodliness and worldly lusts, Titus 2:12 (Moro. 10:32). in damnable heresies, even denying the Lord, 2 Pet. 2:1. antichrist, that denieth the Father and the Son, 1 Jn. 2:22. ungodly men … denying the only Lord, Jude 1:4. hast not denied my faith, Rev. 2:13. kept my word, and hast not denied my name, Rev. 3:8.",
